course: dictionary
lesson: 5441
title: Lampshades and light
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lampshade is the cover that goes over a light bulb on a lamp. Its job is to soften the light and make it look nicer.
explain: Read the clues around a word. «Aroha in Wellington cracked a lampshade trampolining in the lounge and blamed the cat.» Then Mum said, «The cat was at the vet all day.» A cat at the vet cannot have been in the lounge, so Mum knows the cat did not break it. Here the clues show who is telling the truth.
explain: Some lampshades let a little light through, so the light looks soft. Scientists call this translucent. Lampshades can also block, spread or direct light. Paper is a common material for lampshades, but paper should never touch a hot bulb, because it can catch fire.
fact: A lampshade is a cover that goes over a light bulb on a lamp.
fact: A lampshade softens the light and makes the room look nicer.
fact: Some lampshades are translucent, which means they let some light through.
fact: Paper lampshades should not touch hot bulbs, because paper can catch fire.
exercise: What is the main job of a lampshade? | To keep the lamp from falling over | To stop the light from ever coming on | To make the bulb hotter | *To soften the light and make it look nicer
exercise: Mum said, «The cat was at the vet all day.» What does this tell us? | The lampshade was taken to the vet | *The cat could not have broken the lampshade in the lounge | The cat broke the lampshade and then went to the vet | Mum was angry with the vet
exercise: Which word in «Aroha in Wellington cracked a lampshade trampolining in the lounge» names the cover over a light? | lounge | *lampshade | Wellington | trampolining
test: Why should a paper lampshade not touch a hot bulb? | Because the light becomes too bright to see | Because the lampshade will become cold | *Because paper near a bulb can catch fire | Because bulbs only work when nothing touches them
test: In science, what does translucent mean? | *Letting some light through | Making a loud noise | Blocking all light completely | Being very heavy
exam: In «Aroha cracked a lampshade», what does cracked most nearly mean? | Turned on | Cleaned carefully | *Broke, leaving a split or line | Painted
